er"}]}, "margin": {"l": 0, "r": 0, "t": 40, "b": 0}, "title": {"text": "Siberia Arctic Breach (June 2020) (2020-06-20)"}, "annotations": [{"align": "left", "bgcolor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.85)", "bordercolor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.15)", "borderpad": 8, "borderwidth": 1, "font": {"color": "#1a1a2e", "size": 11}, "showarrow": false, "text": "PLANETARY STATE SHIFT. Verkhoyansk hit 38\u00b0C, the highest temperature ever recorded north of the Arctic Circle. While wet-bulb stress was low (dry heat), the *anomaly* was +18\u00b0C above normal, triggering massive peat fires and permafrost melt.<br><br><i>Click 3D Earth for full visualization in Google Earth</i>", "x": 0.02, "xanchor": "left", "xref": "paper", "y": 0.02, "yanchor": "bottom", "yref": "paper"}]}}